# =============================================================================
#  LaTeX build artifacts.
#
#  Everything here is regenerated by `latexmk -pdf main.tex` (or the
#  pdflatex -> bibtex -> pdflatex x2 cycle), so none of it belongs in git.
#  Only main.tex, sections/, figures/ and references.bib are sources.
# =============================================================================

# Core latex/pdflatex output
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.dvi
*.xdv
*.ps

# Bibliography (regenerated by bibtex from references.bib)
*.bbl
*.blg
*.bcf
*.run.xml
*-blx.bib

# latexmk
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.figlist
*.makefile
*.fdb

# Index / glossary
*.idx
*.ilg
*.ind
*.glo
*.gls
*.glg
*.acn
*.acr
*.alg

# SyncTeX (editor <-> PDF cursor sync; local only, and large)
*.synctex.gz
*.synctex(busy)

# Beamer
*.nav
*.snm
*.vrb

# Editor and OS cruft
*.bak
*.tmp
*~
.DS_Store

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The compiled report itself.
#
# main.pdf is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the deliverable, and keeping it in
# the repo means it can be read without a TeX installation. The cost is a ~4 MB
# binary diff on every rebuild. To stop tracking it instead, uncomment the line
# below and run:  git rm --cached report/main.pdf
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# main.pdf
